part of the response. I'll also want to mention that files are saved. I should keep it concise and make sure to include a disclaimer. Being clear and straightforward will help ensure the user understands everything!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I ran the skin cancer pipeline on your image and saved the skill artifacts in the workspace here:\n\n`/home/node/.openclaw/workspace/skin_pipeline_runs/2026-03-31T16-57-26Z`\n\nSaved files:\n- `00_run_summary.json`\n- `01_upload_request.json`\n- `02_upload_response.json`\n- `03_execution_request.json`\n- `04_execution_response.json`\n\nResult summary:\n- Skin cancer class: **Benign nevus**\n- Confidence: **0.9984**\n- Image Analyzer prediction: **nv**\n- CAM coverage: **0.1199**\n- CAM center ratio: **0.9229**\n- CAM left-right asymmetry: **0.5957**\n- CAM top-bottom asymmetry: **0.1383**\n- CAM explanation: the model focused on features described as asymmetry with central structural homogeneity\n- X-AI summary: the image was classified as a **benign nevus** with high confidence\n\nRecommended next steps from the pipeline:\n1. Consult medical literature for further evaluation\n2. Consider other diagnostic possibilities such as atypical nevus or melanoma\n3. Review medical history and perform a thorough physical examination\n\nThis is a **preliminary pipeline signal, not a diagnosis**.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69be3b4593ce5ab1f19b2cfb/a454064c-e7f1-4700-b027-0921cd98b479.jpg\n\nIf you want, I can also extract the raw JSON into a cleaner report file in the workspace.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0a6fe6893dee0bb00169cbfd063e2081918003d8e6cbdecbc5\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":985,"output":409,"cacheRead":16768,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":18162,"cost":{"input":0.0024625000000000003,"output":0.00613